          "id": "SP_TRICHOGORGIA_MUZIKAE_CORDEIRO_2019",
          "name": "Trichogorgia muzikae Cordeiro, 2019",
          "rank": "SPECIES",
          "commonName": "",
          "lineage": "Trichogorgia",
          "subspeciesCount": 0,
          "description": "Small, delicate, uniplanar, flexible flabellate colonies, dichotomously branched, not lyrate, up to 2.8 cm tall and 4 cm wide. Colonies with attachment scars, but lacking calcareous holdfasts. Calcified axis, golden to pale yellow, circular in cross-section (Fig. 4 E), layers concentric (not undulated) up to 0.5 mm in diameter. First order branchlets 0.8 – 3.3 mm long and internodes 3.0 – 7.4 mm long. Polyps verruciform 0.18 – 0.23 mm tall and 0.2 – 0.3 mm wide when contracted, occurring in an alternate manner in two rows along branchlets and rarely on the main stem, slightly turned to one face of the colony, occurring in a density of 10 – 14 polyps / cm. Interpolypar distances from 0.17 proximally, decreasing to 0.04 mm towards branchlet tips. Sclerites present in both polyps and coenenchyme as very flattened smooth eight-shaped scales with a median waist. Main stem usually devoid of polyps and up to 4.6 mm long. Branchlets up to the 6 th order and terminal branches up to 20 mm long. Sclerites show a concentric extinction pattern under polarized light. Polyp body wall with up to eight rows of transversely oriented scales 55 – 100 µm long (81.87 ± 12.98 µm) and 25 – 41 µm wide (32.75 ± 4.86 µm), becoming more irregularly shaped and longitudinally oriented toward the oral portion (Fig. 5 A). Tentacular scales longitudinally arranged, slightly more sculptured, elongate, usually lacking a median waist 50 – 92 µm long (70.57 ± 12.59 µm) and 15 – 27 µm wide (19.43 ± 4.35 µm) (Fig.",
          "sourcedFrom": "gbif",
          "wikipediaTitle": "gbif:10823177",
          "authorship": "Cordeiro",
          "yearPublished": "2019",
